# AGENT TUNER GUIDANCE

> **Reference** for customization patterns, agent-specific input collection, rules/templates decoupling, and architecture compliance

---

## SECTION 1: 7 CUSTOMIZATION DIMENSIONS

| # | Dimension | What Changes | Files Affected |
|---|-----------|--------------|----------------|
| 1 | RISEN Framework | Role, inputs, steps, expectations, narrowing | `{ID}_{Agent}.mdc` |
| 2 | Phase Workflow | Phase count, tasks, checkpoints, state schema | `Phase_Orchestration.mdc` |
| 3 | Guidance Patterns | Domain patterns, naming, few-shot, checklists | `Guidance.mdc` |
| 4 | Stop Points | Phase-specific stops, questions, self-check | `Mandatory_Stop_Points.mdc` |
| 5 | Templates | Style YAML, template guide, section structure | `templates/` |
| 6 | Examples | Reference examples, pattern projects, common modules | `examples/` |
| 7 | Documentation | README, ARCHITECTURE, Production Learnings | Root docs |

### Customization is NOT Just Config

Customization can fundamentally rewrite the RISEN framework, phase structure, guidance patterns, and stop points while preserving the R-GENIE architecture skeleton. The skeleton (4-5 lean rule files, RISEN, phases, stop points, quick reference) MUST be preserved.

