## SECTION 4: RULES TUNING (Phase 4)

### Rules/Templates Decoupling (CRITICAL)

**Before modifying any rule file, verify:**

```
RULES (Generic - Behavioral)          TEMPLATES (Specific - Structural)
├── How to think                      ├── *-style.yaml (section structure)
├── How to interact                   ├── *-template-guide.md (content)
├── When to stop/wait                 └── examples/ (formatting reference)
├── Phase transitions
└── Decision strategies
```

| Content Type | Goes In | NOT In |
|--------------|---------|--------|
| Section numbers, names, structure | `templates/` | `rules/` |
| Diagram placement details | `templates/` | `rules/` |
| Content requirements per section | `templates/` | `rules/` |
| Behavioral guidance | `rules/` | `templates/` |
| Phase workflow, stop/wait | `rules/` | `templates/` |

**Validation before writing rules (agents 01, 02, 05, 06, 07):**
- [ ] Change does NOT contain specific section numbers
- [ ] Change does NOT dictate specific section names
- [ ] Change does NOT specify diagram placement locations
- [ ] Change focuses on behavior/strategy, not content structure
- [ ] If structural → target is templates/, not rules/

### Tuning Sub-Steps

**Attribution Preservation (ALL sub-steps):**
- Preserve `author:` field (original agent author) in frontmatter — do NOT change to tuner's name
- Preserve R-GENIE framework footer + original agent author footer at end of every file
- Tuner attribution line will be appended in Phase 6 (Write & Activate)

**4A. Main Entry ({ID}_{Agent}.mdc):**
- Update RISEN framework (project-specific role, inputs, expectations)
- Update critical rules section
- Update output structure if different
- Keep lean (≤200 lines, `alwaysApply: true`)

**4B. Phase Orchestration:**
- Adjust phase structure if project needs different phases
- Update checkpoint messages with project context
- Update state file schema if new fields needed

**4C. Guidance:**
- Add project-specific patterns to EXISTING sections (append, don't restructure)
- Add few-shot examples (bad→good format)
- Add decision matrices
- Add quality checklist items
- **Respect decoupling**: No section numbers or structural content

**4D. Stop Points:**
- Add project-specific stop points
- Update self-check with project-specific conditions
- Add forbidden/required phrases if needed

**4E. Documentation:**
- Regenerate README.md reflecting customized agent
- Regenerate ARCHITECTURE.md with updated workflow
- Update INDEX.md cross-references and version
- Add project context to Production_Learnings.md header

### Placement Rules (from integrate-production-learnings.md)

| Learning Type | Target | Reason |
|---------------|--------|--------|
| Workflow change | Main .mdc | Affects user flow |
| Error pattern | Guidance | Grouped fixes |
| Best practice | Guidance | General patterns |
| Structure/content change | `templates/` | Template-specific |

- **`alwaysApply: true` files** → Only CRITICAL additions (context cost)
- **Phase-specific** → Add to rule loaded during that phase
- **Match existing style** → Never create new sections without clear need

