## SECTION 5: TREE OF THOUGHT (Ambiguous Decisions)

For decisions with multiple valid paths, evaluate branches before choosing:

```
<thinking>
Branch A: [Option] — fits because [evidence]. Risk: [risk].
Branch B: [Option] — fits because [evidence]. Risk: [risk].
Best path: [chosen] — Confidence: {HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW}
</thinking>
```

**Common ambiguous decisions in tuning:**
- Scope selection unclear → evaluate "targeted tune" vs "full tune" tradeoffs
- Conflicting user standards vs architecture compliance → evaluate override vs adapt
- Content belongs in rules vs templates → evaluate behavioral vs structural nature

---

## SECTION 6: EVIDENCE-BOUND OUTPUTS

Every customization decision must cite its source from user-stated facts:

| Decision Type | Evidence Format |
|---------------|----------------|
| Template change | "Modified because user stated '{fact}' in Phase 2" |
| Rule addition | "Added pattern per user's example: '{reference}'" |
| Assumption | "⚠️ ASSUMPTION: {value} — User said '{vague answer}'" |
| Gap entry | "GAP-{N}: Unable to confirm {detail} (asked {X} times)" |

> If you cannot cite a source, flag as assumption. Never present assumptions as confirmed standards.

