## SECTION 8: RULES TUNING PATTERNS

### Pre-Write Validation (Run before Phase 6)

**Per `lib/docs/AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_STANDARD.md`:**

- [ ] 4 or 5 rule files in `rules/` (depending on template needs)
- [ ] Main entry has RISEN framework (all 5 elements)
- [ ] Main entry has Quick Reference table
- [ ] Phase Orchestration has state machine or phase table
- [ ] Phase Orchestration has `<thinking>` block template
- [ ] Phase Orchestration has Confidence Calibration
- [ ] Guidance has few-shot examples (bad→good)
- [ ] Guidance has Evidence-Bound output citation rules
- [ ] Guidance has Quick Reference table
- [ ] Mandatory Stop Points has anti-patterns and forbidden phrases
- [ ] Mandatory Stop Points has self-check section
- [ ] Mandatory Stop Points has Quick Reference table
- [ ] Each file has version in frontmatter (all matching)
- [ ] `INDEX.md` up to date
- [ ] All cross-references valid
- [ ] DRY compliance: no duplicated patterns/definitions across rule files — each concept has one authoritative source, others cross-reference via `@file.mdc`
- [ ] File sizes within limits
- [ ] For agents 01/05/06: No section numbers in rules
- [ ] README.md exists and reflects current state
- [ ] ARCHITECTURE.md exists and reflects current workflow
- [ ] Original `author:` field preserved in `.mdc` frontmatter (not overwritten by tuner)
- [ ] Dual-author footer preserved (R-GENIE framework + original agent author)
- [ ] Tuner attribution line appended to modified files

> **Reference agent**: Study `examples/reference-agent-01-technical-design/` to understand what a correctly structured R-GENIE agent looks like before validating modifications.

### File Size Limits

| File | Standard | Complex (8+ phases) |
|------|----------|---------------------|
| Main Entry | ≤200 lines | ≤200 lines |
| Template Configuration | ≤250 lines | ≤400 lines |
| Phase Orchestration | ≤350 lines | ≤400 lines |
| Guidance | ≤500 lines | ≤600 lines |
| Mandatory Stop Points | ≤350 lines | ≤450 lines |

If content exceeds limits → move detailed content to `lib/docs/`

### LLM Behavioral Gap Coverage (Optional Validation)

> Before finalizing tuning, optionally read `lib/docs/LLM_BEHAVIORAL_GAPS.md` and verify the tuned agent still addresses the 14 documented LLM behavioral gaps. Use the Summary Matrix and Technique-to-File Mapping sections to confirm no countermeasure was weakened by the tuning.

