## SECTION 9: MERMAID STANDARDS RETROFIT

> **When to apply:** Any tuning session where the target agent emits Mermaid diagrams (rule files or domain deliverables). In practice, every R-GENIE agent qualifies — the standard skeleton alone produces 3+ Mermaid blocks.
>
> **Full playbook:** `lib/docs/customization-patterns.md` §7 "Mermaid Standards Retrofit Pattern" — 12-point diagnostic checklist, 10 ordered retrofit steps, embedding template for the agent's Guidance file, and post-retrofit validation list.
>
> **Canonical rules:** `lib/docs/mermaid-diagram-best-practices.md` — ten non-negotiable rules (mandatory `curve: 'linear'` init directive, `<br/>` not `\n`, declaration-order layout control, arrow semantics, style placement, etc.), adopted from Agent Builder.

### 9.1 Trigger Conditions — When Mermaid Retrofit Is MANDATORY

Propose Mermaid Standards Retrofit (Phase 2 input collection or Phase 4 rules tuning) whenever ANY of these apply to the target agent:

1. The agent's `rules/` contain any Mermaid block (Phase Orchestration state machine, INDEX.md maps, ARCHITECTURE.md flow).
2. The agent's domain outputs include Mermaid diagrams (HLD, flow map, architecture doc, design doc).
3. The agent's current Guidance file has **no** Mermaid Diagram Standards section.
4. The agent's current Stop Points SELF-CHECK has **no** MERMAID RENDERING GUARD item.
5. The agent predates Agent Builder v1.3.6 (first release carrying the full Mermaid standards).

### 9.2 Tuning Flow Summary

```
Phase 2 Input Collection
  ├─ Ask: "Does the agent emit Mermaid diagrams in rules/ or deliverables?" (Yes/No)
  ├─ If Yes → run §9.1 trigger check
  └─ If any trigger → queue Mermaid Retrofit in Phase 4 plan

Phase 4 Rules Tuning
  ├─ Follow customization-patterns.md §7.2 (10 ordered steps)
  ├─ Backup first (§8 Backup procedure)
  ├─ Diagnose all Mermaid blocks via §7.1 checklist
  ├─ Fix diagrams with targeted edit/multi_edit (NEVER sed on Mermaid)
  ├─ Embed §7.3 template in Guidance
  ├─ Embed §12.4 guard (from Agent Builder) in Stop Points
  └─ Validate via §7.4 post-retrofit checklist
```

### 9.3 What Not to Do

- ❌ Do NOT regex-replace across Mermaid blocks — syntax is position-sensitive and structure-critical.
- ❌ Do NOT skip the backup step — Mermaid edits are error-prone.
- ❌ Do NOT combine Mermaid retrofit with unrelated tuning in a single commit — keep the retrofit auditable.
- ❌ Do NOT copy diagrams between agents verbatim — colour palettes should be re-derived per the agent's domain.

